SUMMARY:Yolo Basin Foundation Docent Training
DESCRIPTION:Event Date: October 24 – 25\, 2026 \nYolo Basin Foundation invites you to engage with your community by learning how to lead tours of the Yolo Bypass Wildlife Area and the City of Davis Wetlands. Volunteers who become wetland tour docents lead guided visits through these unique natural areas\, welcoming wildlife enthusiasts\, families\, students\, and retired members of our community. \nTours of the Yolo Bypass Wildlife Area take place October through June on the third Sunday of the month\, from 9:00 a.m. to noon. Tours of the City of Davis Wetlands are offered the first Sunday of the month\, from 9:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m.\, throughout the year. More information about Yolo Basin Foundation’s Wetland Tour program and these unique wetland sites can be found on Yolo Basin Foundation’s website: https://yolobasin.org/wetland-tours/ \nJoin us for this two-day docent training on Saturday\, October 24\, from 9:00 a.m. to 12:30 p.m.\, and Sunday\, October 25\, from 9:00 a.m. to 11:30 a.m. \nEverything you need to know about becoming a wetland tour docent will be covered during this training. To sign up or to learn more\, contact our Community Engagement Coordinator via email at volunteer@yolobasin.org. \nPhoto caption: Sunset at the Yolo Bypass Wildlife Area\nPhoto credit: Rogelio Aguilar Lopez
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/yolo-basin-foundation-docent-training/2026-10-24/
LOCATION:CA
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image-1.jpeg
ORGANIZER;CN="Yolo Basin Foundation":MAILTO:volunteer@yolobasin.org
END:VEVENT
