SUMMARY:Art Sale - Friends of the Davis Public Library
DESCRIPTION:This ONE-TIME stand-alone Art Sale will feature artworks donated by the Davis Arts Center and other sources. The works span many decades and are by a variety of well-and lesser-known artists of our region and beyond\, with many created by artists associated with the well-regarded UCD Art Department from its inception in the late 1950s. \nArtists of work to be included (subject to change) include:\nDavid Gilhooly\, Gregory Kondos\, Dwight Eberly\, James Estey\, Kurt Fishback\, Jack Hooper\, Richard Nelson\, Chiura Obata\, Yoshio Taylor\, Makepeace Tsao\, Sandy Delehanty\, Arthur Gonzalez\, Irene Pijoan\, Mary Foley Benson\, Margery Mann\, James Yeh-Jau Liu and many others. \nThe roughly 200 works include watercolors\, oils\, acrylics\, photography\, prints\, ceramics\, etc. Most works are under $400; many are $50 or less! In addition\, premium art books will be offered\, which have not been featured at monthly book sales. \nUnlike our monthly Book Sales\, the Art Sale will be for ONE DAY ONLY. Sale of these works will help the Friends of the Davis Public Library (FDPL) to fund the Davis Public Library’s programming\, inventory and equipment needs.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/art-sale-friends-of-the-davis-public-library/
LOCATION:Blanchard Room\, Davis Public Library\, 315 E. 14th\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Community,Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/AS-header-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Friends of the Davis Public Library":MAILTO:membership@sbcglobal.net
END:VEVENT
